{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5hr23ffmgU1mKv2rnyJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my exploration, here's my analysis summary:\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions `CREATED` shipments to `CONFIRMED`, idempotently handles already-`CONFIRMED` shipments, rejects `CANCELLED` shipments with 409, and returns 404 for missing shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` (enum ShipmentStatus with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` (POST create, GET by id, GET list)\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` (save, findById, findAll, existsById, clear)\n- ApiExceptions: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- ErrorCode enum: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` (catches ApiException, returns ApiError envelope)\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Error handling pattern: Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler centralizes response formatting to ApiError envelope\n2. Error codes are machine-readable and part of the public API contract (enum ErrorCode)\n3. HTTP status codes: 201 CREATED for POST create, 409 CONFLICT for state violations, 404 NOT_FOUND for missing resources\n4. Repository pattern: In-memory ConcurrentHashMap storage, injected into controller\n5. Testing: MockMvc integration tests with @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc annotations\n6. Response shape: ResponseEntity with appropriate status codes\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — must add the confirm endpoint method\n2. `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — must add new error code for state conflicts (e.g., SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM)\n3. `src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all confirm cases\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Breaking existing tests if endpoint naming or status codes don't match conventions\n2. Forgetting idempotent semantics (already-CONFIRMED must succeed)\n3. Incorrect HTTP status code for CANCELLED case (must be 409, not 400)\n4. Missing the error code in ApiError enum, causing NullPointerException at runtime\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone. The requirement is clear: 404 for missing, 409 for CANCELLED, 200 with updated shipment for success. The only ambiguity was which error code to use for the CANCELLED case, but adding a new one follows the established pattern of specific error codes (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, etc.).\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the ErrorCode enum. This code indicates that a shipment's state prevents the confirm operation (specifically, CANCELLED shipments).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Finds the shipment or throws ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity with the (possibly unchanged) shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Test 1: Confirms a CREATED shipment → transitions to CONFIRMED, returns 200\n   - Test 2: Confirms an already-CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds, returns 200, status unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Test 3: Attempts to confirm a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n   - Test 4: Attempts to confirm non-existent shipment → returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Instead of adding a new error code, reuse VALIDATION_FAILED for the CANCELLED case. Rejected because VALIDATION_FAILED is semantically for input validation errors, not state conflicts. The ErrorCode enum's design is to have specific codes for each failure mode, as evidenced by SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS. A new code keeps the API contract clear.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Status |\n|------|------|-------|----------|--------|\n| Confirm CREATED | findById(id) | save(Shipment with CONFIRMED) | Shipment (updated) | 200 |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | findById(id) | (no save) | Shipment (unchanged) | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | findById(id) | (no save) | ApiError with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM | 409 |\n| Confirm non-existent | findById(id) returns null | (no save) | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 |\n\nAll error cases throw ApiException subclasses, caught by GlobalExceptionHandler and formatted to ApiError envelope.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1 (confirm_CREATED_transitions_to_CONFIRMED)**: Creates S-1 (CREATED), calls POST /shipments/S-1/confirm, asserts status 200 and status field is CONFIRMED\n- **Test 2 (confirm_CONFIRMED_is_idempotent)**: Creates S-2 (CREATED), confirms it (now CONFIRMED), confirms again, asserts status 200 and status field still CONFIRMED\n- **Test 3 (confirm_CANCELLED_rejected_with_409)**: Manually saves a CANCELLED shipment via repository, calls POST /shipments/S-3/confirm, asserts status 409 and error code is SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n- **Test 4 (confirm_non_existent_returns_404)**: Calls POST /shipments/unknown/confirm, asserts status 404 and error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code according to the design.\n\nFirst, add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":257,"cache_read_input_tokens":19509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":257},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8e8d7c7-6486-405e-8b06-332949ae6759","uuid":"782b07d8-89bc-4f34-947b-06699feba2d6","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:33:44.589Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5hr1bdAduZjZzDFqwbp"}
